$sound2text — speech-to-text with OpenAI Whisper

SUMMARY
  Transcribes audio files from sounds[] using the openai-whisper Python package
  (https://github.com/openai/whisper). Writes one texts[] link per input file,
  or a single joined file when join=1.

SYNTAX
  $sound2text
  $sound2text(model='base')
  $sound2text(model='turbo', language='en')
  $sound2text(model='medium', task='translate', language='Japanese')
  $sound2text(model='small', join=1)
  $sound2text(json=True)

INPUT
  sounds[] — required; each link is transcribed (wav, mp3, flac, m4a, etc.)
  prompts[] / instruction body — optional initial_prompt for Whisper (context hint)

OUTPUT
  texts[] — transcript text (.txt per file, or one joined file)
  texts[] — with json=True: .json per file with word-level timestamps

ARGUMENTS
  model=      — Whisper size (default base). Examples: tiny, base, small,
                medium, large-v3, turbo, tiny.en, base.en (English-only, often faster)
  language=   — ISO language code (e.g. en, ru, Japanese). Omit for auto-detect.
  task=       — transcribe (default) or translate (speech → English; use medium/large,
                not turbo — turbo is poor for translation per upstream docs)
  join=       — 1/true: one texts[] entry with all transcripts separated by blank lines
  json=       — 1/true: write .json with full text and words[] ({word, start, end} in seconds)
  count=      — unused unless [n] repeat on the external

DEPENDENCIES
  uv sync --extra sound2text
  ffmpeg on PATH (required by Whisper to load audio)

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_SOUND2TEXT=1 — stub texts, no model load
  AH_EXTERNAL_INPROCESS=sound2text — run in orchestrator process (optional)

MODEL NOTES (from OpenAI Whisper)
  turbo — fast, good for English transcription
  base / small — balance of speed and quality
  medium / large — better for translation and hard audio
  Models download on first use to the Whisper cache (~/.cache/whisper)

BEHAVIOR
  Loads each Whisper model once per process and reuses it.
  Multiple files in sounds[] are processed in order.

EXAMPLE
  @track: @caption -> $music(model='st')
  @lyrics: @track -> $sound2text(model='base')
  @clip: (@images, @lyrics) -> $image_clip

  @transcript: $sound2text(model='turbo', language='en')
  podcast episode text

TROUBLESHOOTING
  ImportError / No module named whisper
    Run: uv sync --extra sound2text
  ffmpeg not found
    Install ffmpeg and ensure it is on PATH
  CUDA out of memory
    Use a smaller model= (tiny, base, small)

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No (prompts[] may be used as initial_prompt only).
